memo_weighing.cfo:
Weighed as my independent check on program estimates [BX-1316]. It is a thin seat: one call, Low confidence beyond the buffer test, and he says his A350 number comes from doctrine and inference.

His binding buffer veto on all 12 fps rows stands, and the fps holds.

On the Re-engine he raised no veto (S4 +1.72 clears his floor by 4.00) and advised hold. I took that advice, but not on his authority. I took it because he gave me the number I asked for and showed his reasons both ways, and it met the condition I set in my frame. At about 30% (range 25-35%) the edge is +0.91, inside epsilon. With his one-year reset carried, it is about +0.6.

His other legs I accept as checked:
- slip leg: two years costs about $0.56B, and it still passes;
- relaunch: a 2045 relaunch is worth +0.3 to +0.74, inside epsilon, so this was the last window;
- cash path and stress net debt: $0.0B for B and the 10-year rows;
- the fps trend: waiting helps at half the pace of discounting.

His premium figures ($0.91B weighted, $2.00B on S1) are the ones I log.

